410	\begin{lemma}[The Pauli question distribution is a typed CL distribution]\label{lem:pauli-question-typed-cl}
411		\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauliQuestionDistribution_eq_typedCL}
412		\uses{def:pauli-question-distribution, def:typed-cl-distributions, def:graph-distribution}
413		Fix an admissible tuple $\mathsf{qldparams} = (q,m,d)$ (Definition~\ref{def:admissible}) and let $L = \{L_t\}_{t \in \mathcal T^{\mathrm{pauli}}}$ be the family of Definition~\ref{def:pauli-question-distribution}. Then the question distribution of $\mathfrak{G}^{\mathrm{Pauli}}_{\mathsf{qldparams}}$ is the $(\mathcal T^{\mathrm{pauli}}, G^{\mathrm{pauli}})$-typed conditionally linear distribution $\mu^{G^{\mathrm{pauli}}}_{L,\,L}$ of Definition~\ref{def:typed-cl-distributions}. As in Lemma~\ref{lem:ld-question-typed-cl}, the linked declaration states the distribution identity alone: an equality between the question sampler of $\mathfrak{G}^{\mathrm{Pauli}}_{\mathsf{qldparams}}$ and the distribution that the construction of Definition~\ref{def:typed-cl-distributions} produces from the pair $(L, L)$ and the graph $G^{\mathrm{pauli}}$, a construction that is available for an arbitrary family of maps. Neither that equality nor the assertion that $L$ is a $\mathcal T^{\mathrm{pauli}}$-typed family of conditionally linear functions is formalized: the Lean proof of the equality is open, and so is the level assertion for the maps $L_t$ listed in Definition~\ref{def:pauli-question-distribution}. Both obligations are tracked as issue~\#180, so the statement and the proof below carry no completion mark.
