548		Let $a, b$ be the universal constants of Theorem~\ref{thm:pauli}, and let $c$ be the smallest \emph{even} integer that is at least $(b+a)/b$. For every integer $R \ge 4$, define the tuple $\mathsf{introparams}(R) = (q, m, d)$ by
549		\begin{itemize}
550			\item $q = 2^k$ for $k = c \lceil \log \log R \rceil + 1$,
551			\item $m = 2^j$, where $j$ is the unique integer with $2^j \le c \lceil \log R \rceil + 1 < 2^{j+1}$,
552			\item $d = 1$.
